--- body ---
## Context

`0912` builds the deterministic half of consolidation: pooling, grouping,
reports, instrumentation. This ticket is the judged half — deciding whether a
group is one lesson, writing the merged body, and landing it.

Similarity never settles the question. Two entries can be near-identical in
wording and record different conditions, which is why roughly half of what
lexical matching proposes is noise. So a model authors here, and the boundary
matters more than the mechanism.

Design reference: "What the model decides, and what it must not" in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/dream/SKILL.md` — the consolidation pass
- whatever `0912` leaves as the grouped-candidate interface

## Actions

1. The model reads a group and decides whether it is one lesson. It writes the
   merged body and declares what the result supersedes.
2. **It decides nothing about retention** — not what ranks, not what expires,
   not what is still true. Those stay deterministic, which is what keeps the
   index reproducible from the store alone.
3. Tombstone the merged originals. They stay readable; that is what makes a
   wrong merge recoverable rather than fatal.
4. Route merges into the harness tier through a pull request. It is the only
   operation that replaces text with different text, and it reaches every
   session.
5. Record the model's identity and its prompt in the run's provenance, beside
   the embedding model's.

## Test

Red first, on fixtures `0912` already ships: the known-genuine pair merges and
the merged body carries `supersedes`; the named lexical false positive
(`dropna_before_merge` / `rebase_before_merge`) is not merged; the straddling
project/harness pair resolves by tombstoning the project copy.

## Verification

- [ ] No merge applies without confirmation
- [ ] Merged originals are readable after the merge
- [ ] Provenance carries model identity and prompt

## Invariants

- Nothing is deleted. Merged originals are tombstoned.
- Promotion moves up into the harness tier and never back out.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The three fixtures pass: genuine pair merged with `supersedes`, named
      false positive refused, straddling pair tombstoning the project copy
- [ ] Harness-tier merges are PR-routed, proven by the routing not by prose
- [ ] Model identity and prompt in provenance
